|passage=See’st thou yon river, whose translucent wave,<br>Forth issuing from the darkness, windeth through<br>The argent streets o’ th’ City, '''imaging'''<br>The soft inversion of her tremulous Domes,}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Old Curiosity Shop|71|page=210|text=Sorrow was dead indeed in her, but peace and perfect happiness were born; '''imaged''' in her tranquil beauty and profound repose.}}
